menu "Zigbee Light"

    config ZL_DEBUG
        bool "DEBUG mode (prototype on USB)"
        default n
        # Keep the CPU awake while USB is connected, so flashing and the
        # console keep working. Light sleep is then only simulated,
        # see power_management.c.
        select USJ_NO_AUTO_LS_ON_CONNECTION
        help
            Primary build switch of this project.

            y = DEBUG / prototype: ESP32-H2 board powered via USB for flashing
                and debugging. The light chain is simulated by the on-board
                WS2812 (RMT driver).
            n = production: the light chain is driven by an external LED
                driver (constant current source) via LEDC PWM and a boost
                converter enable pin.

            Light sleep: while the USB Serial/JTAG port is connected, the
            CPU does not enter automatic light sleep
            (selects USJ_NO_AUTO_LS_ON_CONNECTION). Whether the 802.15.4
            radio still sleeps between keepalives in that case is not
            documented. Without USB connection the device sleeps for real.

            Further debug-only behaviour is keyed off this option as well
            (C macro APP_DEBUG in app_config.h).

    config ZL_DEBUG_LIGHT_SLEEP
        bool "Allow automatic light sleep in DEBUG builds"
        depends on ZL_DEBUG
        default n
        help
            n (default): DEBUG builds never enter automatic light sleep, so
            USB flashing and the console always work.
            y: light sleep as in production, except while the host sends
            USB SOF packets (USJ_NO_AUTO_LS_ON_CONNECTION). Caution: if the
            host suspends the USB port (e.g. Windows selective suspend after
            closing the monitor), the chip sleeps and the USB Serial/JTAG
            stops responding (no light sleep support on ESP32-H2). Flashing
            then needs download mode (hold BOOT, press RESET).

    config ZL_DEBUG_BATTERY_PERCENT
        int "Emulated battery level in % (DEBUG)"
        depends on ZL_DEBUG
        range 0 100
        default 95
        help
            DEBUG builds have no battery measurement (USB powered). This value
            is reported as BatteryPercentageRemaining (Power Configuration
            cluster) instead of "unknown" (0xFF), so Zigbee2MQTT / Home
            Assistant show a battery level. BatteryVoltage stays unknown.

endmenu
